  {"i":3452,"t":["actions","shopping"],"n":"お使い is mainly a shopping errand, so 'work' fits loosely at best; actions already covers the 'use/user' sense, so no sense entry is needed."},
  {"i":3454,"t":["family"],"n":"Losing a spouse or child through death is taught in the family unit; 'feelings' is only an association."},
  {"i":3469,"t":["time"],"n":"ついで(に) means occasion or 'while you're at it', which belongs with time. 'Qualities' does not fit, and it is not a grammar or degree word, so 'function' does not apply."},
  {"i":3487,"t":["numbers","function"],"n":"Learners meet it as 'roughly/approximately' with amounts. The 'briefly/cursorily' sense is still an adverb, so a separate qualities sense entry is unnecessary."},
  {"i":3594,"t":["communication","language"],"n":"聞き取る is the listening skill (聞き取り) taught in communication and language units; the 'inquire' sense also fits communication."},
  {"i":3600,"t":["business"],"n":"The word is mostly used for a marketing target or target group; 'sports' is a loose association."}
